IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc4-industrial-injuries-general`

-- TESTS for ssc4-industrial-injuries-general.l4 (ss 94-101; s 102 is blank in this text). Expected values are written from the text beside each assertion.

§ `Tests -- ss 94 to 101`

§§ `s 94 -- right to industrial injuries benefit`

-- s 94(1): payable "where an employed earner suffers personal injury caused ... by accident arising out of and in the course of his employment, being employed earner's employment". All four: of the kind (TRUE). Any missing: "where" is not "only if", so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 94(1) the personal injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 94(1) the personal injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 94(1) the personal injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)` (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 94(1) the personal injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 94(1) the personal injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 94(1) the personal injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)` NOTHING TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 94(1) the personal injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 94(1) the personal injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 94(1) industrial injuries benefit is payable` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 94(1) industrial injuries benefit is payable` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 94(1) industrial injuries benefit is payable` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 94(2): "Industrial injuries benefit consists of the following benefits": disablement benefit, reduced earnings allowance, retirement allowance, industrial death benefit. "Consists of" closes the list: any other benefit is not part of it.
#ASSERT `s 94(2) the benefit is part of industrial injuries benefit` `disablement benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 94(2) the benefit is part of industrial injuries benefit` `reduced earnings allowance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 94(2) the benefit is part of industrial injuries benefit` `retirement allowance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 94(2) the benefit is part of industrial injuries benefit` `industrial death benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 94(2) the benefit is part of industrial injuries benefit` `attendance allowance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(2) the benefit is part of industrial injuries benefit` `short-term incapacity benefit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(2) the benefit is part of industrial injuries benefit` `Category A retirement pension` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(2) the benefit is part of industrial injuries benefit` `unemployability supplement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(2) the benefit is part of industrial injuries benefit` `child benefit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(2) the benefit is part of industrial injuries benefit` `Christmas bonus` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 94(3): an accident arising in the course of the employment is taken, "in the absence of evidence to the contrary", also to have arisen out of it. With evidence to the contrary the presumption does not run (JUST FALSE, for this subsection only: fork F6); not in the course, the subsection is silent (NOTHING).
#ASSERT `s 94(3) the accident is taken to have arisen out of the employment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 94(3) the accident is taken to have arisen out of the employment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(3) the accident is taken to have arisen out of the employment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 94(3) the accident is taken to have arisen out of the employment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 94(5): "Subject to sections 117, 119 and 120 below, industrial injuries benefit shall not be payable in respect of an accident happening while the earner is outside Great Britain." Outside, no exception: barred. An exception that applies: no bar. Inside Great Britain: the bar is not engaged (FALSE, fork F8). An exception unknown: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 94(5) the person is barred from industrial injuries benefit for an accident outside Great Britain` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 94(5) the person is barred from industrial injuries benefit for an accident outside Great Britain` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(5) the person is barred from industrial injuries benefit for an accident outside Great Britain` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(5) the person is barred from industrial injuries benefit for an accident outside Great Britain` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(5) the person is barred from industrial injuries benefit for an accident outside Great Britain` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(5) the person is barred from industrial injuries benefit for an accident outside Great Britain` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 94(5) the person is barred from industrial injuries benefit for an accident outside Great Britain` TRUE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 94(5) the person is barred from industrial injuries benefit for an accident outside Great Britain` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 94(5) the person is barred from industrial injuries benefit for an accident outside Great Britain` TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(5) the person is barred from industrial injuries benefit for an accident outside Great Britain` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(5) the person is barred from industrial injuries benefit for an accident outside Great Britain` FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(5) the person is barred from industrial injuries benefit for an accident outside Great Britain` FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 94(6): "work" in the contexts "incapable of work" and "incapacity for work" means work which the person can be reasonably expected to do. Incapable of work he can reasonably be expected to do: incapable of work in this sense. Incapable only of work he cannot be expected to do, or not incapable: not. Outside the following provisions of this Part: the definition does not speak.
#ASSERT `s 94(6) the person is incapable of work, "work" meaning work the person can reasonably be expected to do` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 94(6) the person is incapable of work, "work" meaning work the person can reasonably be expected to do` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(6) the person is incapable of work, "work" meaning work the person can reasonably be expected to do` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(6) the person is incapable of work, "work" meaning work the person can reasonably be expected to do` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94(6) the person is incapable of work, "work" meaning work the person can reasonably be expected to do` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 94(6) the person is incapable of work, "work" meaning work the person can reasonably be expected to do` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 95 -- relevant employments`

-- s 95(1): "employed earner's employment" is taken "to include" any employment by virtue of which a person is, or is treated by regulations as being, an employed earner. Neither: "include" is not "means", so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 95(1) the employment is employed earner's employment` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95(1) the employment is employed earner's employment` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95(1) the employment is employed earner's employment` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95(1) the employment is employed earner's employment` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 95(1) the employment is employed earner's employment` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 95(1) the employment is employed earner's employment` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 95(1) the employment is employed earner's employment` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 95(3): an employment is employed earner's employment in relation to an accident "if (and only if)" it is, or is treated by regulations as being, such an employment when the accident occurs.
#ASSERT `s 95(3) the employment is employed earner's employment in relation to the accident` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95(3) the employment is employed earner's employment in relation to the accident` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95(3) the employment is employed earner's employment in relation to the accident` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95(3) the employment is employed earner's employment in relation to the accident` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 95(3) the employment is employed earner's employment in relation to the accident` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 95(3) the employment is employed earner's employment in relation to the accident` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 95(3) the employment is employed earner's employment in relation to the accident` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 95(4): "in relation to any time before 6th April 1975" the references are to "insured person" or "insurable employment". 5 April 1975 is before; 6 April 1975 and later are not before, and the subsection is silent.
#ASSERT `s 95(4) the reference is construed as a reference to an insured person or insurable employment` (Date 5 4 1975) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95(4) the reference is construed as a reference to an insured person or insurable employment` (Date 1 1 1970) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95(4) the reference is construed as a reference to an insured person or insurable employment` (Date 6 4 1975) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 95(4) the reference is construed as a reference to an insured person or insurable employment` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 95(5): "the industrial injuries and diseases provisions" means (a) s 95 and ss 96 to 110; (b) other provisions of this Act so far as they relate to those sections; (c) provisions of the three named enactments so far as they so relate. "Means" closes the list.
#ASSERT `s 95(5) the provision is among the industrial injuries and diseases provisions` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95(5) the provision is among the industrial injuries and diseases provisions` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95(5) the provision is among the industrial injuries and diseases provisions` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95(5) the provision is among the industrial injuries and diseases provisions` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95(5) the provision is among the industrial injuries and diseases provisions` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 95A -- employment training schemes etc`

-- s 95A(1): "any reference to employed earner's employment shall be taken to include participation in an employment training scheme or employment training course of a prescribed description". Prescribed: included. Not prescribed, unknown, or no participation: "include" is open, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 95A(1) the participation is employed earner's employment` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95A(1) the participation is employed earner's employment` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 95A(1) the participation is employed earner's employment` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 95A(1) the participation is employed earner's employment` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 95A(2): a reference to an employer, in relation to such participation, "shall be taken to be a prescribed person". Prescribed person in such a case: the employer. Otherwise the subsection does not say who is not.
#ASSERT `s 95A(2) the person is the employer in relation to the participation` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95A(2) the person is the employer in relation to the participation` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 95A(2) the person is the employer in relation to the participation` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 95A(2) the person is the employer in relation to the participation` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 95A(2) the person is the employer in relation to the participation` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 95A(3): the term has the same meaning as in section 95: the same answers as s 95(5).
#ASSERT `s 95A(3) the provision is among the industrial injuries and diseases provisions` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95A(3) the provision is among the industrial injuries and diseases provisions` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95A(3) the provision is among the industrial injuries and diseases provisions` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 95A(3) the provision is among the industrial injuries and diseases provisions` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 97 -- accidents in course of illegal employments`

-- s 97(3): "relevant employment" means (a) for an accident, the employment out of and in the course of which the accident arises; (b) for a prescribed disease or injury, the employment to the nature of which it is due.
#ASSERT `s 97(3) the employment is the relevant employment` `s 97(3) an accident` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 97(3) the employment is the relevant employment` `s 97(3) an accident` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 97(3) the employment is the relevant employment` `s 97(3) an accident` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 97(3) the employment is the relevant employment` `s 97(3) an accident` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 97(3) the employment is the relevant employment` `s 97(3) a prescribed disease or injury` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 97(3) the employment is the relevant employment` `s 97(3) a prescribed disease or injury` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 97(3) the employment is the relevant employment` `s 97(3) a prescribed disease or injury` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 97(3) the employment is the relevant employment` `s 97(3) a prescribed disease or injury` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 97(1) and (2): where a claim is made, or an application under s 29 of the Social Security Act 1998, "The Secretary of State may direct that the relevant employment shall ... be treated as having been employed earner's employment notwithstanding that" the contract was void or the earner not lawfully employed. Claim or application, direction, and illegality: treated. Anything missing: the section does not say, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 97(2) the relevant employment is treated as employed earner's employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 97(2) the relevant employment is treated as employed earner's employment` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 97(2) the relevant employment is treated as employed earner's employment` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 97(2) the relevant employment is treated as employed earner's employment` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 97(2) the relevant employment is treated as employed earner's employment` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 97(2) the relevant employment is treated as employed earner's employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 98 -- earner acting in breach of regulations, etc.`

-- s 98: taken to arise out of and in the course of the employment "if (a) the accident would have been taken so to have arisen had the act not been done in contravention ...; and (b) the act is done for the purposes of and in connection with the employer's trade or business". Both: TRUE. Either fails: FALSE for the section. (a) unknown with (b) met: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 98 the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 98 the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 98 the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 98 the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 98 the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 98 the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 99 -- earner travelling in employer's transport`

-- s 99(2): "references to a vehicle include a ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft". A ship etc. is a vehicle here. Another conveyance: "include" is open, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 99(2) the conveyance is a vehicle for the purposes of this section` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 99(2) the conveyance is a vehicle for the purposes of this section` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 99(1): a passenger travelling with permission to or from work by a vehicle is taken to be in the course of employment "if (a) the accident would have been taken so to have arisen had he been under such an obligation; and (b) ... the vehicle (i) is being operated by or on behalf of his employer or some other person by whom it is provided in pursuance of arrangements made with his employer; and (ii) is not being operated in the ordinary course of a public transport service".
#ASSERT `s 99(1) the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 99(1) the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 99(1) the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 99(1) the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 99(1) the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 99(1) the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 99(1) the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 99(1) the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 99(1) the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 99(1) the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 100 -- accidents happening while meeting emergency`

-- s 100: taken to arise out of and in the course of the employment "if it happens while he is taking steps, on an actual or supposed emergency at those premises, to rescue, succour or protect persons ... or to avert or minimise serious damage to property". Premises, emergency, and either purpose: TRUE. Premises but no emergency or no such purpose: FALSE. Not at the premises: the sentence is not engaged, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 100 the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 100 the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 100 the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 100 the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 100 the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 100 the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 100 the accident is taken by this section to arise out of and in the course of the employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 101 -- accident caused by another's misconduct etc.`

-- s 101: an accident "happening after 19th December 1961" is treated as arising out of the employment, "where it would not apart from this section be so treated", "if (a) the accident arises in the course of the employment; and (b) the accident either is caused (i)... (ii)... (iii)... or is caused by or consists in the employed earner being struck by any object or by lightning; and (c) the employed earner did not directly or indirectly induce or contribute".
